  "_about_carry_cases": [
    "Carrying the loop wire when a stage is appended after the tail (#189 S4, #331; spec 1.5 item 6): the editor's rule, ui/src/components/flows/flowsSlice.ts carryLoopWire, which compile.py does not have, because the server only reads the wire.",
    "graph: the flow before, the stage about to be appended already on the canvas and unwired. connect: the one wire the operator draws, out of the lane's tail into the new stage, with the id the caller mints ('drawn' in these cases). block: the TARGET whose lane it is.",
    "result: the flow after the connect, in one write: the drawn wire last, and every pass wire into the block's next that left a stage of its lane re-sourced to the lane's new tail, keeping its id and its place. Nothing else changes.",
    "lane_tail: the block's tail in the result. loop_wires: the ids compile.py loop_wires finds in the result, in edge order.",
    "Graded by server/tests/test_flows_panel_lane.py (the result is a valid graph, lane_tail and loop_wires as recorded, lane_refusals is empty, and the result is the graph plus the drawn wire with only pass wires into the block's next re-sourced) and by ui/src/components/flows/__tests__/panelLane.test.ts (carryLoopWire makes result) and flowsSlice.test.ts (flowsConnect makes result, in one graph write)."
  ],
